    "name": "azul_widgets_sounds_every_request_of_the_sound_board_is_recorded_with_its_route",
    "description": "The Sounds section under AZ_BACKEND=headless (a headless window plays nothing and records every request of play_system_sound). A press of a sound button (the texts of the buttons are unique on the page: a click finds the first text node that CONTAINS its text) asks for that sound; assert_sound counts the REQUESTS, which is the same on every platform, while the route a request takes differs (Android: the AudioManager click, iOS: a haptic, a desktop: none). The recording keeps the request of a sound that did not play too, with the reason, so a second press within the sound's minimum interval is a request that was dropped, not one that was never made. A haptic button is not a sound.",
